<h2 id=3D"system-interconnect">System Interconnect</h2>
<p>The ACES compute nodes are interconnected with NDR200 links.  The leaf a=
nd core switches are interconnected with NDR (400Gb) links in a fat tree to=
pology with a 2:1 oversubscription factor.</p>
<p><img alt=3D"This screenshot shows a diagram of the network interconnect =
for ACES. On the left it shows a representation of the Lustre file system. =
Next to Lustre it shows a collection of 4 infiniband network nodes. There i=
s a connection from the Lustre icor to one of the network nodes. Below the =
inifinband nodes, it shows a colletion of compute nodes with various conect=
ions from and to the infiniband nodes. To the right of the this it shows a =
vertical collection of support nodes. There are also connections from some =
of the infiniband nodes to the support nodes." src=3D"https://hprc.tamu.edu=
/kb/assets/images/aces_all.png" title=3D"ACES Interconnect"></p>
<h2 id=3D"data-transfer-nodes">Data Transfer Nodes</h2>
<p>ACES has two 100Gb data transfer nodes that can be used to transfer data=
 to
ACES via the Globus Connect web interface or Globus command line. Globus
Connect Server v5.4 is installed on the data transfer nodes. One data
transfer node is dedicated to ACCESS users and its collection is listed
as =E2=80=9CACCESS TAMU ACES DTN=E2=80=9D.</p>
<h2 id=3D"usable-memory-for-batch-jobs">Usable Memory for Batch Jobs</h2>
<p>While nodes on ACES have 512 GB of RAM, some of this
memory is used to maintain the software and operating system of the
node. In most cases, excessive memory requests will be automatically
rejected by SLURM.</p>
<p>ACES nodes will have a memory limit of 488 GB per node for batch jobs.</=
p>
